chx:input a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "input"@en ; rdfs:domain rd:IOExample ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> ; skos:definition "The Python expression of an input-output example, as text that the checks execute."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:output a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "output"@en ; rdfs:domain rd:IOExample ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> ; skos:definition "The value that the input of an input-output example evaluates to, as text."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:refersTo a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "refers to"@en ; rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_ReferenceByName ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section when the account of the first names the thing that the second illustrates and draws on it: the same rule one level up, the tamper test, the release check, the list of BIP 39, the seed of BIP 32, the descriptor of a backup, the PSBT. It says that the first account points to the second; it states no cause and no need."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Reused: dcterms:references says that a resource points to another; the category records that the account names the thing by its name and that the name is carried as a link, never as a string. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the words that state it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE, section 3, the category Reference by name (under the syntactic relationship); construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:hasConsequence a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has consequence"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Causal ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section when the account says that what the first illustrates brings about what the second illustrates: a payment that reveals no secret and the traffic that needs no encryption, the new seed of an encrypted wallet and the backup that is stale at once."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No standard relation was reused: the Relations Ontology could not be opened in this run, so none was checked against the account. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the words that state it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE, section 3, the category Causal relationship; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:isComparedWith a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is compared with"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Comparative ;
    skos:definition "Links two examples of different sections when the account sets what they illustrate side by side, as alike or as different: the same lesson of a lost key and a lost passphrase, the same error of a wrong order and a missing descriptor, a stretch compared with the rounds of BIP 39, a PIN that makes the guesser wait compared with a file attacked offline, a coin with a hologram compared with a printed paper wallet, secret sharing compared with multisignature."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Symmetric, so the link is stated once and holds both ways. No standard relation says a comparison. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the words that state it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE, section 3, the category Similarity and opposition (Comparative); construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:buildsOn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "builds on"@en ; rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/dc/terms/requires> ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Requirement ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates something the first one needs in order to hold: the loss of one key of three is survived only if the descriptor is kept. It differs from refers to (a name is not a need) and from has consequence (the needed thing is not the cause of the first)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Reused: dcterms:requires says that a resource is required by another to support its function or coherence, which is what the sentence of the link says. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the words that state it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE, section 3, the category Requirement; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:isEarlierThan a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:AsymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is earlier than"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_TemporalOrder ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section when the dates the two accounts give put what the first illustrates before what the second illustrates: the sale of the physical coins until November 2013 before the closing of the exchange in early 2014."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "OWL-Time's before was not reused: it joins temporal entities (instants and intervals) and the ends here are examples that carry dates. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the words that state it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE, section 3, the category Temporal order; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:qualifies a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "qualifies"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Epistemic ;
    skos:definition "Links the example that records what was not run to the example of another section whose claim it limits: the claim of the second is read from a page or a document and not from a run, and the first example says so. It states a limit of knowledge about the second example, not a cause and not a need."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No standard relation was reused: none of the standard properties checked says that an account limits the claim of another; the citation relations of CiTO join publications and were not checked against examples. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the words that state it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE, section 3, the category Epistemic and argumentative relationship; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
